  "feedback_interpretation": "Round-4 feedback confirmed large methylquinoline underprediction at 10/1 and large high-ratio V2 underprediction for two phenols. Acetoxybenzaldehyde showed opposite V1 error directions at 5/1 and 10/1. The multifunctional ester was closer at 1/1, and oxime errors changed from overprediction at 10/1 and 20/1 to underprediction at 50/1; this batch therefore prioritizes condition transitions and chemical contrasts. The tert-butylbenzoate result weakened the earlier broad benzoate-bias hypothesis, so no benzoate was selected. Current CW rows remain unmeasured. V2\u2212V1 is elution interval width, not uncertainty.",
